    "summary": "Scarlet>Fire, Looks Like Rain, and a lively New Orleans encore shine",
    "blurb": "The first set delivers strong numbers like Looks Like Rain and Might As Well before launching into a seamless Scarlet Begonias → Fire on the Mountain transition that fuels an explosive second half. Highlights include Terrapin Station, The Wheel, Throwing Stones and a vibrant encore featuring New Orleans and Big Boss Man.",
    "review": "June 21, 1984 at Kingswood Music Theater captured one of those summer‑solstice shows where the Dead were clearly in a good mood. The opening half is anchored by solid performances of Looks Like Rain and Might As Well, but it’s the second set that truly shines – a flawless Scarlet Begonias into Fire on the Mountain segue sets up a rolling groove through Terrapin Station, an extended Drum‑Space excursion, and a powerful closing trio of The Wheel, Throwing Stones and Not Fade Away. The encore brings a joyous New Orleans jam and a gritty Big Boss Man, amplified by The Band’s guest appearance, leaving the crowd dancing into the night.\n\nFrom a listening perspective the best experience comes from the high‑quality audience tape (gd1984-06-21.nak300...), which preserves the room’s energy while delivering clear instrument separation. While the FM matrix capture offers crisp detail, its treble‑heavy mix buries Phil’s bass and Brent’s keys. Overall, the show balances tight musicianship with that unmistakable Dead spontaneity – a solid 4½‑star outing worth revisiting.",
